/** * @file * Customizing Hero Image tutorial template. * * Available
variables: * - tutorial: The tutorial definition. * - images_path: Path to the
tutorial images. */ #}
{% set header_content %}
<p>
  The IBM API Connect Developer Portal enables you to personalize the hero image
  on your site’s front page. By customizing this image, you can better reflect
  your brand identity and create a more engaging experience for developers
  browsing your APIs.
</p>

<p>
  In this tutorial, we’ll guide you through the process of generating a custom
  sub-theme, adding a new hero image, applying custom CSS, and uploading the
  updated theme to your portal.
</p>

<p>This tutorial covers the following steps:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Generating a sub-theme</li>
  <li>Adding a custom hero image</li>
  <li>Styling the hero image in <code>override.css</code></li>
  <li>Uploading and enabling the sub-theme</li>
</ul>

<img
  src="{{ images_path }}/current-hero.png"
  alt="Current Hero Image"
  class="img-responsive"
  loading="lazy"
/>
{% endset %}

{% set steps_content %}
<li class="gs-step" data-step="Generate Sub-theme">
  <h3>Step 1: Generate a Sub-theme</h3>
  <p>1. Navigate to:</p>
  <div class="path-instruction">
    <strong>Appearance → Generate sub-theme</strong>
  </div>
  <p>2. In the <strong>Generate</strong> tab:</p>
  <ul class="instruction-list">
    <li>
      Enter a <strong>Subtheme name</strong> (e.g., <code>my_theme</code>)
    </li>
    <li>Select <strong>CSS</strong> as the Subtheme type</li>
    <li>Select <strong>Default Connect Theme</strong> as the base template</li>
  </ul>
  <p>3. Click <strong>Generate</strong>, then download and extract the ZIP file</p>
  <p>Once your sub-theme is set up, you’ll be able to apply custom styles directly to your portal.</p>
</li>

<li class="gs-step" data-step="Add Hero Image">
  <h3>Step 2: Add Your Custom Hero Image</h3>
  <p>1. Download an image to use as your hero banner. For example, you can use 
    <a href="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1562705121-e624542c7b9b?q=80&w=3270&auto=format&fit=crop&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxwaG90by1wYWdlfHx8fGVufDB8fHx8fA==" target="_blank">
      this sample image
    </a> or choose one from your own collection.
  </p>
  <p>2. Save the image in your sub-theme’s <code>images</code> folder and name it 
    <code>welcome-banner.png</code> for easy reference.
  </p>
</li>

<li class="gs-step" data-step="Customize Hero Image with CSS">
  <h3>Step 3: Customize the Appearance with CSS</h3>
  <p>1. Open the <code>override.css</code> file in your sub-theme folder.</p>
  <p>2. Add the following CSS to style the hero image:</p>

  <div class="command-block">
    <pre><code class="language-css">.welcomebanner {
  background: url('../images/welcome-banner.png') no-repeat center center;
  background-size: cover;
  min-height: 400px;
  display: flex;
  color: #ffffff;
  text-align: center;
}</code></pre>
  </div>
</li>

<li class="gs-step" data-step="Verify Theme Structure">
  <h3>Step 4: Verify the Theme Structure</h3>
  <p>After adding your CSS and hero image, your sub-theme folder should look like this:</p>

  <div class="command-block">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">your-theme/
├── css/
│   ├── mail.css
│   ├── override.css
├── images/
│   ├── ibmcarbon/svg/ErrorPages
│   ├── welcome-banner.png
├── theme-settings.yml
├── your-theme.libraries.yml
├── your-theme.theme
├── your-theme.info.yml
├── composer.json
├── favicon.ico
├── logo.svg
└── screenshot.png</code></pre>
  </div>

  <div class="success-message">
    <p>Your sub-theme is now ready for upload.</p>
  </div>
</li>

<li class="gs-step" data-step="Upload and Enable Theme">
  <h3>Step 5: Upload and Enable the Theme</h3>
  <p>1. Zip the contents of your sub-theme folder (including the 
    <code>override.css</code> file and <code>welcome-banner.png</code>).
  </p>
  <div class="command-block">
    <pre><code class="language-bash">zip -r mycustomtheme.zip mycustomtheme</code></pre>
  </div> 
  <p>2. Navigate to:</p>
  <div class="path-instruction">
    <strong>Appearance → Add new theme</strong>
  </div>
  <p>3. Upload your sub-theme zip file.</p>
  <p>4. After installation, click <strong>Enable newly added themes</strong>.</p>
  <p>5. Find your theme under <strong>Disabled themes</strong> and click<strong> Enable and set as default</strong>.</p>

  <img
    src="{{ images_path }}/enable-theme.png"
    alt="Enable Uploaded Theme"
    class="img-responsive"
    loading="lazy"
  />

  <div class="success-message">
    <p>Your custom sub-theme has been uploaded and activated!</p>
  </div>
</li>

<li class="gs-step" data-step="Check Result">
  <h3>Step 6: Check the Result</h3>
  <p>Refresh the front page of your portal. The new hero image should now appear as your welcome banner, giving your Developer Portal a branded, custom look.</p>

  <img
    src="{{ images_path }}/updated-hero.png"
    alt="Updated Hero Image on Portal Front Page"
    class="img-responsive"
    loading="lazy"
  />

  <div class="success-message">
    <p>Congratulations! You’ve successfully customized your portal’s hero image.</p>
  </div>
</li>
{% endset %}

{% include 'tutorial-base.html.twig' with { 'tutorial': tutorial, 'images_path': images_path, 'header_content': header_content, 'steps_content': steps_content } %}
